    {
      "id": "claim_e8bed59435dd48fa97e2bf364fcc175a",
      "statement": "EmuThread uses core Run and Pause in response to control state. Its condition-variable waits permit a stop request and, on the running path, a pending shader-cache reload. It detaches the debugger and shuts down the guest process when the thread exits.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/qt_common/render/emu_thread.cpp#L48-L78",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:53088f3f6f625723beae54f24800556ee24d48cbb719aae068b5c698a69f98f6:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_0f123c2d82dc47968f3776a293786069",
      "statement": "SDL_AppInit creates a backend-specific EmuWindow_SDL3, prepares the filesystem and calls System::Load. SDL_AppEvent forwards events to the window, while SDL_AppIterate applies pending window titles and decides whether the application should continue. This frontend shares core emulation but has its own window and event loop.",
